1. Introduction

Smart City Public Safety project predicts the emergency level of incidents using machine learning techniques.

2. Objective

    Build predictive classification models.
    Predict emergency levels.
    Compare multiple supervised learning algorithms.
    Evaluate model performance using classification metrics, confusion matrix and ROC-AUC.

3. Dataset
    Records: 9,800
    Features: 13 predictive features after removing Incident_ID and target
    Target: Emergency_Level
    Classes: Low, Medium, High

4. Algorithms Used
    Logistic Regression
    Decision Tree
    Random Forest
    Support Vector Machine (SVM)

5. Data Preparation
    Cleaned dataset from Task 1 was used.
    Categorical features were label encoded.
    Target variable was encoded.
    Dataset split into 80% training and 20% testing.
    StandardScaler was used for feature scaling.

6. Evaluation Metrics
    Accuracy
    Precision
    Recall
    F1 Score
    Confusion Matrix
    ROC-AUC

7. Results
    ==================================================
    Best Model
    ==================================================
    Model        Logistic Regression
    Accuracy                0.994898
    Precision               0.994917
    Recall                  0.994898
    F1 Score                0.994874
    Name: 0, dtype: object

8. Conclusion
The project demonstrates the use of supervised machine learning for predicting emergency levels in a smart city public safety environment. Multiple classification algorithms were trained and compared using standard evaluation metrics. The best-performing model was selected based on the evaluation results. Confusion matrix and ROC-AUC analysis were also used to understand model performance.